  "summary": {
    "intent": "Fix apps/validate's broken react-docgen-typescript oracle by giving it a TypeScript 6 API separate from typescript@next, build the semantic probe and parity check, then build the Rust tsc-client for the Lifecycle gate and commit it with an ADR.",
    "outcome": "The RDT oracle was fixed and the probe and parity scripts were added, reproducing the Evidence numbers on the full corpus. The crates/tsc-client crate was built, mutation-tested and reviewed, then committed in two commits (crate, then ADR 0007 plus doc updates). The exit gate returned a process-level fail, and its two blockers were addressed before committing.",
    "learnings": {
      "repo": [
        "apps/validate is a Node/TS harness where console.log is the convention; the Rust CLI's no-println rule (crates/cli/AGENTS.md) does not apply to it.",
        "pnpm workspace `overrides` did not rewrite react-docgen-typescript's typescript peer resolution. Aliasing `typescript-next: npm:typescript@next` as a direct dependency and keeping `typescript@^6.0.3` for RDT worked.",
        "typescript@next exposes a JS async API via `typescript/unstable/async` (API, SignatureKind, SymbolFlags). SyntaxKind is in `typescript/unstable/ast`, and plain file-path strings work as document identifiers.",
        "oxlint enforces no-await-in-loop and no-nested-ternary in apps/validate; oxfmt is the formatter.",
        "Callisto moved its semantic-model docs from .claude/ to docs/architecture (commit a3351846c) because only Claude Code could find them there.",
        "The large uncommitted pile at session start (AGENTS.md rename, .agents/.codex/.cursor dirs, ADR 0006) came from one earlier session, 233bd878.",
        "tsc-client design: a session owns its child's I/O. A single writer task takes whole frames from a bounded 16-frame channel, and `closed` is set once via OnceLock. CloseOnDrop guards close the session on task exit, and restart is decided from `closed()`.",
        "Root-level mutants.out/ and mutants.out.old/ are gitignored leftovers from Sep 26."
      ],
      "code": [
        {
          "path": "crates/tsc-client/src/client.rs",
          "line": 257,
          "finding": "The request send is `write_tx.send(body).await`, which is cancel-safe. Swapping it for try_send was caught by the 24-request timeout test."
        },
        {
          "path": "crates/tsc-client/src/client.rs",
          "line": 134,
          "finding": "The writer's stop branch (`stop_writer.notified() => return`) lets shutdown wake a writer blocked mid-write. A new test covers it, and it fails when the line is deleted."
        },
        {
          "path": "crates/tsc-client/src/supervisor.rs",
          "line": 165,
          "finding": "Restart is decided from `closed()`, not from JoinHandle state."
        }
      ],
      "workflow": [
        "Delegated implementer, reviewer and exit-gate subagents plus cargo-mutants gave strong verification, but they were slow and hit the memory reaper.",
        "Subagent hand-backs must be treated as reports, not authority. The harness flagged settings-json patterns that were only git status listings.",
        "Timing-sensitive async tests need a multi-thread runtime and widened bounds. On a single-threaded runtime, 24 synchronous 1 MiB serializations delayed timers and made the test flaky.",
        "A fake child must reproduce real process behavior. The noisy_stderr fake had to exit when a stderr write fails, or the mutant survived.",
        "Verify shell loops actually ran the test. One flake-hunting loop was meaningless because the `ls` alias rejected `-t`.",
        "Stage only the files you own, since the working tree contained unrelated pending changes."
      ]
    },
    "friction": [
      "The `react-docgen-typescript` peer dependency on typescript@7 crashed on import (ts.JsxEmit undefined). The pnpm override did not take effect, and several install and lockfile attempts were needed.",
      "The exit gate ran nearly an hour and returned an interim result several times, with the machine low on memory. The memory reaper killed a background command and a mutation rerun at 115 of 125 mutants.",
      "The exit gate reported one unexplained failure of one_failing_call_does_not_affect_a_concurrently_in_flight_sibling in an isolated copy. It could not be reproduced in 40 normal runs or under CPU load.",
      "Spec AC-12 (`exit_after:1:7`) was unachievable because the restarted child also exits after one answer. The spec had to be revised to use `fatal_frame_once_then_echo`.",
      "A persisted mutants2 report still listed spawn_stderr_drain as MISSED after the fix, so it was stale.",
      "git status briefly looked as if something had been committed, which prompted a check."
    ],
    "open_items": [
      "Lifecycle items still open: header-size cap, stderr that isn't UTF-8, honoring handshake_timeout, recovery after the restart cap trips, and whether a restarted request may replay.",
      "The tsc-client is not wired into crates/core, the CLI or the NAPI binding, which waits on the doc's 'Open decisions'.",
      "Cost needs re-measuring through the Rust client. Step 4 of the original doc was intentionally left for later.",
      "Hand mutants P13 and P14 and about 10 framing.rs mutants were never run. Writer-mid-write stop, Write-vs-Crashed, and the post-insert re-check race have weak or no coverage.",
      "The unrelated uncommitted pile (AGENTS.md migration, .agents/.codex/.cursor/.gemini scaffolding, ADR 0006, .claude/semantic-model regeneration, and hook/settings changes) still needs its own commit or PR.",
      "The oracle-fix work (apps/validate, docs, pnpm-lock) was proposed as its own commit but the transcript doesn't show it committed.",
      "The AC-12 spec revision was made in the scratchpad spec JSON only. Whether it counts as recorded through scribe:correct-spec is unverified.",
      "Whether .claude/semantic-model should move to docs/architecture, as Callisto did, is undecided."
    ]
  },
